[0.0, "o", "\u001b[0m\u001b[31m \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[90mJev can judge it from the file's own text, so a RULE.md with the Must and Never examples (the inline || chain versus\u001b[0m\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[90m isAuthorized(user)) is enough.\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[0m\u001b[31m \u001b[38;5;156m◇\u001b[0m  Jev reads the code\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b[31m \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[90mThe crammed statements and compound conditions are visible in the file's own syntax, so neither types nor other \u001b[0m\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[90mpackages or dependents are needed to judge it.\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n"]
