[0.0, "o", "em for\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m        array-method callbacks, such as \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215m.filter((line) => line.length > 0 && !line.startsWith(\"#\"))\u001b[39m\u001b[49m. Say that \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215m??\u001b[39m\u001b[49m is\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m        not a check.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m     \u001b[36m4. \u001b[0m\u001b[1mDecide two edge cases and state them:\u001b[22m\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m          \u001b[36m• \u001b[0mIs a callback inside a condition one call or joined checks? For example, \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mif (x.some((c) => a && b))\u001b[39m\u001b[49m. \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215m\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m            \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mrequire-safety-comment-for-type-assertion.ts:26-30\u001b[39m\u001b[49m was left unflagged.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m          \u001b[36m• \u001b[0mMay a ternary's test join checks? For example, \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mno-known-value-widening.ts:45\u001b[39m\u001b[49m and \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215m\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m            \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mno-unknown-type-aliases.ts:8\u001b[39m\u001b[49m. The current exemption's example has only a single-check test.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m     \u001b[36m5. \u001b[0m\u001b[1mSay whethe"]
