[0.0, "o", "\u001b[0m\u001b[31m \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  The rule should carry no `include` or `exclude` filters. It is better off judging every file Jev reads, because it \r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  is about how statements and conditions are laid out, and that applies to every TS/TSX file in the repo. The trial \r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  found violations everywhere it looked.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  - **Where the findings are:** 23 findings in 100 files, spread over `common/tooling/oxlint` (most of them), the root\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m   `scripts/`, and `sdk/` (alchemy, aws, scripts). No folder came out clean in a way that would justify scoping the \r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  rule to the others.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  - **No extension filter needed:** the files selected for the trial are already only `.ts`/`.tsx`. For example, \r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  `shadcn-ui-registry/packages/consumer-fixture/scripts/check-css.mjs` was left out, as were the manifests and docs. A\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m   `paths` glob for extensions would add nothing.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  - **Excluding the shadcn components does"]
[0.0, "o", "n't hold up:** `shadcn-ui-registry/packages/ui/src/components/ui/**` looked \r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  like a candidate, since `scripts/ui-add.ts` can replace those files with upstream's version when run with \r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  `--overwrite`. But that folder also holds the kit's own components (`banner.tsx`, `stat.tsx`, `status-dot.tsx`, \r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  `button-element.tsx`), so excluding it would silently hide real code. The trial also found the upstream files nearly\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m   clean. Their one finding, in `chart.tsx` at the lowest probability in the report (0.82), points at a filter \r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  callback rather than a condition or a second statement, so it looks like a false positive.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  - **No `content` filter:** the rule doesn't depend on any package or import.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  The trial only covered the first 100 of 283 eligible files, in alphabetical order, so it stopped partway through \r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  `shadcn-ui-registry`. Anything after that, such as `skills/` or `template"]
[0.0, "o", "/`, was never judged. Narrowing scope now \r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  would rest on less evidence than it seems.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
