[0.001, "o", "\u001b[0m\u001b[31m \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  The rule is precise but misses a lot. It flagged 30 of the 100 files. Every flagged line I opened is a real\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  violation, and I found no false positives. It skipped at least 5 judged files with clear violations, and almost\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  every finding names only one line per file.\u001b[0m\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[1mWhat it catches correctly\u001b[22m\u001b[0m\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m    \u001b[36m• \u001b[0m\u001b[1mBody on the condition's line:\u001b[22m \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mcommon/scripts/build-package.ts:12\u001b[39m\u001b[49m, \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mno-known-value-widening.ts:36\u001b[39m\u001b[49m, \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215m\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m      \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mrequire-file-comment.ts:45\u001b[39m\u001b[49m, \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mvite.config.ts:52\u001b[39m\u001b[49m.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m    \u001b[36m• \u001b[0m\u001b[1mJoined checks in a condition:\u001b[22m \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mno-runtime-typeof.ts:59-60\u001b[39m\u001b[49m, \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mWorkloadIdentity.ts:126-129\u001b[39m\u001b[49m (the condition spans\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m      several lines) and \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b["]
[0.0, "o", "38;5;215mdashboard.tsx:40\u001b[39m\u001b[49m.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m    \u001b[36m• \u001b[0m\u001b[1mBoth at once:\u001b[22m \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mno-module-mocking.ts:52\u001b[39m\u001b[49m, \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mno-widen-then-assert.ts:230\u001b[39m\u001b[49m.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m    \u001b[36m• \u001b[0m\u001b[1mThe weakest hit\u001b[22m is \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mdashboard.tsx:40\u001b[39m\u001b[49m at 0.81: \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mevent.key === \"k\" && (event.metaKey || event.ctrlKey)\u001b[39m\u001b[49m. It's correct\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m      by the rule's wording, but it's the kind of line where people will question whether the rule is too strict.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m    \u001b[36m• \u001b[0m\u001b[1mFive hits don't tell you much.\u001b[22m The rule's own examples were copied from these lines: \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mcheck-one-version.ts:348\u001b[39m\u001b[49m, \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215m\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m      \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215morganization.ts:25\u001b[39m\u001b[49m, \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mconsumer-fixture/src/main.tsx:9\u001b[39m\u001b[49m, \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mstat.tsx:175\u001b[39m\u001b[49m, \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mno-shape-in-symbol-names.ts:25\u001b[39m\u001b[49m. They on"]
[0.0, "o", "ly\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m      show the judge recognises its own examples, not that the rule generalises.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[1mMisses (false negatives)\u001b[22m\u001b[0m\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m    \u001b[36m• \u001b[0m\u001b[1mFiles judged with no finding:\u001b[22m\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m        \u001b[36m• \u001b[0m\u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mno-reflect-get.ts:21\u001b[39m\u001b[49m and \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mno-reflect-apply.ts:21\u001b[39m\u001b[49m: \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mif (a || b) return;\u001b[39m\u001b[49m breaks both halves and is almost the\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m          \"Never\" example.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m        \u001b[36m• \u001b[0m\u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mno-conditional-empty-object-spread.ts:41\u001b[39m\u001b[49m: a same-line guard.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m        \u001b[36m• \u001b[0m\u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mdependency-cruiser/src/index.ts:61\u001b[39m\u001b[49m: \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mif (directories.length === 0) return \"(?!)\";\u001b[39m\u001b[49m has the same shape as the\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m          rule's own \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mif (values.length === 0) return null\u001b[39m\u001b[49m.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m        \u001b[36m• \u001b[0m\u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mchart.tsx:1"]
[0.0, "o", "64\u001b[39m\u001b[49m, \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215m210\u001b[39m\u001b[49m, \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215m378\u001b[39m\u001b[49m, \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215m414\u001b[39m\u001b[49m: joined conditions with braced bodies.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m    \u001b[36m• \u001b[0m\u001b[1mOne line per file:\u001b[22m grep counts about 35 same-line bodies in \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mdictionary-types.ts\u001b[39m\u001b[49m, 22 in \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215m\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m      \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mno-known-value-widening.ts\u001b[39m\u001b[49m and 19 in \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mno-widen-then-assert.ts\u001b[39m\u001b[49m, yet each gets one line in the report. Someone\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m      fixing from the report would fix one line per file. This looks like a limit of how adhere reports findings, not\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m      of the rule's wording.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m    \u001b[36m• \u001b[0m\u001b[1mExpect noise if installed at \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215merror\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[1m:\u001b[22m grep (a rough count, test files included) finds about 150 same-line bodies\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m      and 130 single-line joined conditions in the scanned folders.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  "]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1mChanges to the wording and examples\u001b[22m\u001b[0m\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m     \u001b[36m1. \u001b[0m\u001b[1mSplit it into two rules.\u001b[22m The name says \"one statement per line\", but half the rule bans joined checks, which\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m        is a separate concern. For example: \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mstyle/one-statement-per-line\u001b[39m\u001b[49m and \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mstyle/named-predicate-conditions\u001b[39m\u001b[49m, each\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m        with a one-clause description. The misses fall under both halves, so this is for clarity; I can't show it\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m        fixes the misses.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m     \u001b[36m2. \u001b[0m\u001b[1mReplace the examples with code from outside the trial files,\u001b[22m or leave those files out of the next trial.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m        Otherwise the next trial again overstates how well the rule generalises.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m     \u001b[36m3. \u001b[0m\u001b[1mDecide about braces.\u001b[22m The body says \"Give the body braces and a line of its own\", but the description only asks\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m        for the body on the lines after the condition. \u001b[48"]
[0.0, "o", ";5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mgroup-prefixed-files.ts:10-15\u001b[39m\u001b[49m and \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mno-object-parameters.ts:58-59\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m        put a body on the next line without braces, and no finding names those lines. Either add \"in braces\" to the\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m        description and a braceless case to \"Never\", or remove the brace requirement.\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m     \u001b[36m4. \u001b[0m\u001b[1mSay whether a ternary's test may join checks.\u001b[22m As written, \"a conditional expression that picks a value\"\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m        exempts \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mreturn a === null || b === undefined || … ? name : null\u001b[39m\u001b[49m (\u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mno-unknown-type-aliases.ts:8-12\u001b[39m\u001b[49m, \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215m\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m        \u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;215mno-module-mocking.ts:55-62\u001b[39m\u001b[49m). That is the same reading problem the rule targets, so extend the rule to cover it\r\n \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m        or keep the exemption deliberately and say so.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[0m\u001b[31m \u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  common/scripts/build-package.ts: 1 finding\u001b[0m\r\n"]
